    <h1>Shingle Roof Cost by State</h1>

    <!-- Direct Answer Box -->
    <div class="direct-answer">
      <strong>How Geographic Location Affects Roof Replacement Costs:</strong> Across the United States, replacing a residential asphalt shingle roof on an average 2,000 square foot home ranges from approximately <strong>$7,400 to $18,500</strong>. Regional pricing is heavily driven by prevailing skilled trade labor wages, local building permit fees, cold-climate ice dam mandates, and hurricane windborne debris codes.
    </div>

    <h2>51-State Shingle Roof Replacement Cost Table</h2>
    <p>
      Estimated ranges for a standard 2,000 sq ft home (approx. 25 squares of architectural asphalt shingles) including single-layer tear-off, synthetic underlayment, and standard permits:
    </p>

